window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY=window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY||{};window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY["ui-infrastructure"]=[{"body": "Read-only pass done; nothing was changed. No `SkillTreeD4*` code exists yet. Paths are abbreviated:\n\n- `R` = `/Users/t8g-2410-pn-005/Documents/MyProject/HELLSCRIPT/wt-d4-skill-plan`\n- `P` = `R/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation`\n- `T` = `R/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Editor`\n- `E` = `R/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Editor`\n- `D` = `R/Docs/Design/D4SkillTree`\n\nThe worktree already has someone else's uncommitted edits: `D/extract.js` and `D/skill_tree_d4.json` are modified, and `D/golden/` is untracked (layout, viewmodel, anatomy and interaction JSON, `styles.json`, `fx.json`).\n\n## 1. DRAWING PRIMITIVES\n\n**API (Graphic local space, y up, unless noted)**\n\n- **`UiMesh`** (`P/UiButtonFace.cs:156-256`) is a static class writing into a `VertexHelper`, so it needs a `MaskableGraphic` host.\n  - `Inset(Rect,n)`, `Box(m,Rect,upper,lower)`, `Frame(m,Rect,n,c)`\n  - `RoundedBox(m,Rect,radius,upper,lower)`, `RoundedRing(m,Rect,radius,width,ink)`\n  - `Gradient(m,Rect,cut,Func<float,Color>,bands=6)` fills a chamfered rect with colour = f(y).\n  - `Ring(m,Rect,cut,width,c)` is a chamfered outline.\n  - `Diamond(m,Vector2,radius,c)`, `Brackets(m,Rect,n,arm,c)`\n  - Rounded shapes use a fixed 24-point contour (`RoundedContour` :174) with no AA. `RoundedContour`, `Gradient` and `Brackets` allocate arrays or Lists on every call.\n- **`UiButtonFace : MaskableGraphic`** (:10) is added by `UiButton.Configure(role,chosen,locked)` (`P/UiButton.cs:28-42`).\n  - `Show(role,chosen,locked,available,hovered,pressed,focused,instant)` (:27) is a no-op when nothing changed. `SetChrome(Gilt|Minimal)`.\n  - It draws a chamfered gradient face, hairline ring, top light, rising glow, and for Primary a double line plus lozenges.\n  - The Tab role is a gradient strip, bottom bar, gold bar and diamond (:84-98). Minimal chrome uses `RoundedBox/RoundedRing` with radius <= 5 (:127-142).\n  - The fade is `Time.unscaledDeltaTime/UiTheme.ButtonFade` (.085 s) (:43-49).\n- **`UiTheme`** (`P/UiTheme.cs:8-130`):\n  - Hex consts at :12-21 (Void, Background, Inset, Panel, Raised, Hover, Selected, Border, Edge, GoldDeep, Gold, GoldBright, Text, Muted, Faint, Success, Danger, Primary). Matching `Color` properties come from `StorageSurface.Hex`.\n  - `Tint(hex,alpha)` :44, `Title/Heading/Body/Caption = 20/15/12/10` :50, `Scale(Rect)` :54.\n  - `ButtonPalette(role,chosen,locked,available,hover,pressed)` returns `UiButtonPalette{top,bottom,edge,light,accent,glow}` (:80; struct at `P/UiButtonFace.cs:149`). `MinimalButtonPalette` :115. `Button/Choice/Skin/Backdrop`.\n  - There are no steel, ember, line-state or rim-gradient tokens.\n- **`UiLayout`** (:148-163):\n  - `Rect(name,parent)`.\n  - `Place(r,x,y,w,h)`: top-left anchor and pivot, y down, size >= 1.\n  - `Stretch(r)`.\n  - `Text(parent,name,value,x,y,w,h,int size,Color,Font font=null)`.\n  - `Clear(parent)`: SetActive(false) plus Destroy.\n- **`UiWindowFrame : Image`** (`P/UiWindowFrame.cs:9`; fields `header, footer, corners`) draws a gradient panel, header band, border and gilt `Brackets` (no dots). `Divider(m,x0,x1,y,n,c,strength,jewel,hole)` (:39) fades its ends and has a centre diamond. `UiHeaderRule.Attach(Transform header)` :61.\n- **`UiIconButton`** (`P/UiIconButton.cs:11`) has `Create(parent,name,icon,x,y,w,h,Action click,framed=true,Color? tint=null,bool backdrop=false,string folder=null,Rect? uv=null)` (:15) and `CreateGlyph(...)` (:23). Both return a `UiButton`.\n- **`SkillIconView`** (`P/SkillIconView.cs:10`):\n  - `Create(parent,passive)` :18, `SetKind`, `SetSkill(id,squareFrame=false)` :48, `SetSprite`.\n  - Children are Plate (an `Image` with a stencil `Mask`), Icon, Cover (Radial360 cooldown) and Frame.\n  - `SkillIconAssets.TryResolve(id,out passive,out sprite)` (:57) only knows ids that `ClassSkills.Find` returns, plus legacy atlas ids.\n- **`SkillTreeGraphic`** (`P/SkillTreeGraphic.cs:25`):\n  - Builder API: `Create(parent,name,x,y,w,h)` :32, `Bind(UiButton)`, `Line(a,b,width,c,hot)`, `Disc`, `Ring`, `Glow(center,inner,outer,c)` (radial halo), `Diamond`, `DiamondRing`, `Box(x,y,w,h,top,bottom)`.\n  - `Link(a,b,crossing,width,c)` is orthogonal, three segments only.\n  - Coordinates are top-left px, and the whole shape list is re-emitted on every dirty.\n  - A private `Polygon(...,sides,start)` (:98) exists. `SkillTreeLayout` :13 is the legacy 37-node placement.\n- **`HuntEdictSurface : Image`** (`P/HuntEdictSurface.cs:9`): `Paint(skin)` :16 (named skins :20-62); public `fill, edge, radius, edgeWidth, underline`. It draws a rounded fill, ring and 1 px AA feather (:80-84). `radius=100` gives a pill.\n- **`StorageSurface : Image`** (`P/StorageSurface.cs:8`): `top,bottom,edge,bottomOnly,sidesOnly,dashed,inset`, `Paint(upper,lower,border)`, `Hex(string)`. Square corners and a 1 px edge. Dashes are a fixed 3/3 px on straight edges (:37-46).\n- **Others:**\n  - `StorageGlyph`: 24-unit line icons by `symbol`.\n  - `UIRectBorder` (BaseMeshEffect), `UiLockGraphic`.\n  - `AttendanceClaimGlow`: static radial glow plus 6 rays.\n  - `TutorialAnchorRing`.\n  - `EquipmentRevealGraphic`: Frame = L corners plus diamond dots (:16-29).\n  - `TitleFrameGraphic/TitleOrnament`.\n  - `RuneGemMesh` (`mainTexture` override :12, rune atlas): public `Hex/Circle/Quad/Line/Outline(points,width,color,dashed)/Polygon(points,light,dark)`.\n  - `TownCircleGraphic` (`P/TownJoystick.cs:52`), `ForgeMilestoneRing`.\n  - `SelectionRune` and `SelectionGroundShadow` (`P/CharacterSelectionStage.cs:95,106`).\n  - `VignetteGraphic` (`P/TutorialCinematic.cs:181`).\n  - `TrainingDpsChart`: polyline plus private dashed/dot helpers (:49,:54).\n  - `DialogueReveal : BaseMeshEffect` (`P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:243`).\n\n**Feature support**\n\n| Feature | Closest existing | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| Vertical gradient fill | `UiMesh.Box/Gradient/RoundedBox`, `StorageSurface.top/bottom` | yes |\n| Gradient (gilt) border | every ring is single colour; `Divider` fades alpha only | no |\n| Rounded rect, per-widget radius | `RoundedBox/RoundedRing(radius)`, `HuntEdictSurface.radius` | yes (one radius for all corners; AA only in HuntEdictSurface) |\n| Dashed outline | `StorageSurface.dashed` | partly (straight edges, 1 px, fixed 3/3) |\n| Dashed line | `RuneGemMesh.Outline(dashed)` (4.5/7.3), `TrainingDpsChart.Dashed` (private) | partly |\n| Hexagon medallion | `SkillTreeGraphic.Polygon` and `RuneBoardGraphic.Hex` are private; `RuneGemMesh.Hex` is atlas-bound | no (no usable public one) |\n| Segmented arc / conic ring | none | no |\n| Soft outer glow / box-shadow | `SkillTreeGraphic.Glow` (circular), `AttendanceClaimGlow`, 1 px feather | partly |\n| Inner shadow | `StorageSurface.inset` (hard 1 px), `UiButtonFace` top light | partly |\n| Blurred backdrop art | no blur code or shader | no |\n| Polyline with glow under-stroke | `Line/Link`; the two-pass wide-translucent plus narrow stroke is at `P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:52` | partly (orthogonal only, no joins or caps) |\n| Corner ornaments (L plus dots) | `UiMesh.Brackets`, `EquipmentRevealGraphic.Frame` | partly |\n| Gradient text / text shadow | Unity `Shadow`/`Outline` | no / yes (hard offset) |\n| Circle / square crops | `SkillIconView` | yes (fixed radius, hard stencil edge) |\n| Scroll plate and panel body | see section 3 | yes, single axis only |\n| Tab buttons | `UiButtonRole.Tab` | partly (gold, not ember) |\n| One-shot FX | see section 5 | partly |\n\n**GAPS and the idiomatic way to fill each**\n\n1. **Gradient rims** (`GILT_RIM` and `STEEL_RIM` are 5-stop vertical gradients): add a `RoundedRing(..., Func<float,Color> byY)` overload to `UiMesh`, mirroring `Gradient`. Put the stop arrays in `UiTheme`, which is exempt from the colour lint.\n2. **Hex, conic arc, angular gradient**:\n   - The design's HEX is a regular pointy-top hexagon, so `Polygon(…,6,90)` already draws it.\n   - Add `UiMesh.Hex`/`HexRing` and `UiMesh.Arc(m,center,rIn,rOut,startDeg,sweepDeg,Func<float,Color> byAngle,segments)`.\n   - Expose them as new `Kind`s in `SkillTreeGraphic` (builder style).\n3. **Polyline with joins, round caps, dash, glow under-stroke, partial range** (ignite and glint): add a new `PolylineGraphic : MaskableGraphic` per state colour, as plan 9.7 says. Give it `SetRange(t0,t1)` and preallocated buffers; reuse the dash maths of `RuneGemMesh.Outline`.\n4. **Rounded dashed outline**: add `UiMesh.DashedRing` walking the `RoundedContour` perimeter.\n5. **Box-shadow, inner shadow, radial plate gradients**:\n   - Add `UiMesh.Glow/Inner(m,Rect,radius,spread,Color)`: a ring from the inflated contour to the rect with an alpha ramp, generalising the feather at `P/HuntEdictSurface.cs:80-84`.\n   - For radial fills, use ellipse fans like `SelectionGroundShadow`.\n   - `RectMask2D` clips glows at the plate edge.\n6. **Blur and CSS filters** (blur 14-18 px art, grayscale/brightness on locked icons):\n   - Add one UI shader under `Resources/`, modelled on `Resources/GlobalHudFade.shader`. It has Stencil and `_ClipRect`, so it works under `Mask`/`RectMask2D`.\n   - Fold in `_Tone` (brightness, saturation) from `Resources/Art/PuzzleHubTone.shader`. That shader has no stencil or clip, so it must not be used inside a scroll plate.\n   - Own the `new Material(shader)` per window and destroy it (`P/PuzzleHubWindow.cs:37,223`).\n   - Icons are 1254², `isReadable:0`, no mips (`W01.png.meta`), so CPU or baked blur is out, and plan §16 forbids resizing icons.\n7. **Gradient text**: add a `TextGradient : BaseMeshEffect`. `DialogueReveal.Conceal` (`P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:243-261`) already rewrites per-glyph vertex colours. Add it before `Shadow` so the shadow copies stay black. Soft text glow is only possible by approximation (`Outline` or several `Shadow`s).\n8. **Dotted corner ornaments and centre diamond rule**: compose `Brackets` + `Diamond` + a new `UiMesh.Disc`. Draw them on a layer above the scroll mask, because the design draws them outside the clip.\n9. **Icon crops with exact radius and dim/desaturate**:\n   - `mask-square` has a fixed radius of about 13%, decoded from its alpha.\n   - Add a textured rounded-rect `MaskableGraphic` with UVs, like the `RuneGemMesh.mainTexture` pattern. This avoids a stencil `Mask` per icon.\n10. **FX**: build them from items 2 and 3 plus `CanvasGroup`/`canvasRenderer.SetAlpha`, `localScale`, a skewed quad inside `RectMask2D` for the shine, and a small pool of `Text` for \"+1\".\n\n## 2. CUSTOM-UNIT ADAPTER WINDOWS\n\n- **Unit.** `BlacksmithWindow.Reflow` (`P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:61-72`):\n  - `safe=UiSafeArea.Current`, `landscape=safe.width>safe.height`, `scale=UiTheme.Scale(safe)`. That formula is min(w/800,h/450) landscape and min(w/405,h/720) portrait (`P/UiTheme.cs:54`).\n  - Canvas units are `width=safe.width/scale` and `height=safe.height/scale`.\n  - :67 sets `U=Clamp(landscape?Min(width/75.8f,height/35.7f):Min(width/31.7f,height/64.5f),8,17)`. Those constants are the HTML's em extents.\n  - `E(em)=em*U` and `Z(em)=Max(7,Round(em*U))` (`P/BlacksmithWindow.Chrome.cs:14,16`).\n  - `RuneBoardWindow.Render` uses the same constants on `shell.Frame.rect` (`P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:62-63`).\n  - Neither fits a fixed design rect or centres margins. The plan §9.2 fit-and-centre 1:1 unit is new code.\n- **Root and canvas.**\n  - Blacksmith creates `new GameObject(\"Blacksmith\",typeof(RectTransform),typeof(Canvas),typeof(CanvasScaler),typeof(GraphicRaycaster))` under the GameUI transform, `ScreenSpaceOverlay`, `sortingOrder=320` (:30-31). Storage is 320, HuntEdict 310, RuneMaster 330.\n  - The scaler is `ConstantPixelSize` with `scaleFactor=scale` (:68).\n  - Reflow does `Clear(canvasRoot)` (destroys all children), adds a backdrop, then a `frame` anchored bottom-left at `safe.position/scale` with `RectMask2D` (:69-71).\n  - On the host stack the host rewrites sorting to `400+i*10` and restores it on removal (`P/ContentWindowHost.cs:87,62`).\n  - RuneBoard owns no canvas. `ContentWindowView.Open` (`P/ContentWindowView.cs:23-29`) builds it, and `Repaint` sets scaler and `Canvas.scaleFactor` (:38-40). `Render` hides the shell title, close, frame and scroll (`P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:64`).\n- **Reflow** is polling, not events: `if(safe!=UiSafeArea.Current||language!=Loc.Language||Mathf.Abs(textScale-readingScale())>.001f)Reflow();` (`P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:40`; same in `P/StorageWindow.cs:72-73`, `P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:56`). Shell windows do it in `ContentWindowView.Update` (:30). `GameUI.ApplyLanguage` also repaints a fixed list of windows (`P/GameUI.cs:109`). `readingScale` is always 1 (`P/GameUI.cs:71`).\n- **Attach.** `ContentWindowHost.Attach(Component owner,Action back,bool pause=true,bool blocksGameplay=true)` (:28) silently returns if the window is not under GameUI (:30). `StoreViewBinding.Attach(Component owner,GameStore store,Action refresh,Func<bool> ready=null,Func<string> visibleState=null)` is at `P/StoreViewBinding.cs:13`. Full real example, `P/StorageWindow.cs:67` and `:111-114`:\n```\nContentWindowHost.Attach(view,view.Escape);StoreViewBinding.Attach(view,store,view.Repaint,()=>view.modal==null&&!view.Dragging,view.DisplayKey);\nstring DisplayKey()=>string.Join(\"|\",StoreViewBinding.EquipmentKey(Account),Account.gold,Account.premium,Account.materials,\n  Account.gemCapacity,StoreViewBinding.Key(Account.warehouseCapacity),...,StoreViewBinding.Key(Account.contentUnlocks),badge?.Invoke());\n```\n  The Blacksmith call has no key (`P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:33`) and is grandfathered at `R/tools/check_ui_refresh.py:60-63`.\n- **Back, pause, input.**\n  - `Push` adds a `CanvasGroup`, takes a ref-counted pause lease on the active `RunState`, and disables interaction on every other canvas under the host. Only the top window is interactable (`P/ContentWindowHost.cs:33-89`).\n  - Escape calls the top entry's `back` (:92-96). `ContentWindowHost.BackLocked` can veto (:22; set at `P/GameUI.TutorialStaging.cs:35`). Close with `Detach(this)`.\n  - Inside the window, repaints are deferred while input is busy. `StoreViewBinding.InputBusy` (:43-50) covers press, `UiButton.Pressed`, a focused InputField and an open dropdown. RuneBoard defers repaint to `LateUpdate` while dragging (`P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:39-43`).\n- **ADAPTERS entries** (`R/tools/check_ui_contract.py:16-23`):\n```\n'BlacksmithWindow': ('ContentWindowHost.Attach','UiTheme.Scale','EquipmentSlotView','CharacterEquipmentView','ItemDetailView'),\n'HuntEdictWindow': ('ContentWindowHost.Attach','UiTheme.Scale','HuntEdictSummary','Session.Draft'),\n'RuneMasterWindow': ('ContentWindowHost.Attach','UiFonts.Body'),\n```\n  Tokens are searched in comment-stripped source of `Owner.cs` plus `Owner.*.cs` (:51-58).\n- **Alternative route.** `RuneBoardWindow` (not in ADAPTERS) uses `ContentWindowView.Open` as its shell, so it needs no canvas exemption. The cost is hiding shell chrome (:64).\n\n## 3. SCROLLING AND INPUT\n\n- **Scroll views.**\n  - All are `ScrollRect` + clear `Image` + `RectMask2D` viewport, content anchored top, `Clamped`. Copies are at `P/ContentWindowView.cs:48-53`, `P/BlacksmithWindow.Controls.cs:32-42` (with `Scrollbar`), `P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:265-277`, `P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:101-106`.\n  - All set `horizontal=false`, except `HudStatusScroll` (horizontal only, no inertia, `P/StatusStripView.cs:10-17,41`) and the codex tab strip (`P/MonsterCodexWindow.cs:100`).\n  - No ScrollRect with both axes exists.\n  - Nested scroll is avoided by locking the outer one (`P/MonsterCodexWindow.Detail.cs:14`, `P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:186`).\n- **Tap vs drag.**\n  - `UiButton` (`P/UiButton.cs:12-97`) has no drag logic. It relies on EventSystem, so a ScrollRect drag cancels the press. `Pressed` (:24) lets `StoreViewBinding` postpone repaints.\n  - Custom cells forward gestures to the parent ScrollRect: `StorageCell` (`P/StorageWindow.Drag.cs:13-31`, with `!e.dragging` on click), `RuneMasterCell` (`P/RuneMasterWindow.Drag.cs:7-17`).\n  - Direction arbitration: `TrainingChartView` hands off when `|dy|>|dx|` (`P/TrainingChartView.cs:73-76`). `AttendanceSwipeTarget` decides after 10 px with a 1.25 ratio (`P/AttendanceSwipe.cs:32-53`).\n  - `HoldPress` separates a tap (< 0.3 s) from a 0.7 s hold gauge (`P/HoldPress.cs:8-39`).\n  - `useDragThreshold` is set per control; `pixelDragThreshold` is never changed.\n- **Scroll preserved across Repaint** is the owner's job. Save `content.anchoredPosition.y`, rebuild, `Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases()`, clamp, restore. See `P/ContentWindowView.cs:33,62`, `P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:188-195` (dictionary by key), `P/StorageWindow.cs:440-449`, `P/InventoryWindow.cs:77-79`.\n  - Only Y is ever stored. X is never persisted anywhere.\n  - `StoreViewBinding` restores focus, not scroll (:25-39).\n  - Scroll-into-view: `P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:298-306`, and the smoke `Tap` (`P/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:54-65`).\n  - `UiVisibility.Visible/Fraction` (`P/UiVisibility.cs:13-28`) computes the reachable part of a control.\n\n## 4. TEXT\n\n- **`UiLayout.Text`** (`P/UiTheme.cs:156-160`) sets `font??UiFonts.Body`, int `fontSize`, `supportRichText=true`, `raycastTarget=false`, `horizontalOverflow=Wrap` and `verticalOverflow=Truncate`. It leaves the default UpperLeft alignment, no `lineSpacing`, and does not call `Loc.T`.\n  - `HuntEdictWindow.Text` also runs `ClassSkillTree.Display` (`P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:70`), which swaps skill codes like W01 for names (`Runtime/Core/ClassSkillTree.cs:120`).\n  - Adapters build their own Text, mostly with `supportRichText=false` (`P/BlacksmithWindow.Controls.cs:16-20`).\n- **Fonts** (`P/UiTheme.cs:131-147`):\n  - `Body` is an OS dynamic font from {Apple SD Gothic Neo, Malgun Gothic, Noto Sans CJK KR, Noto Sans CJK, Droid Sans Fallback, Arial}. WebGL uses the preloaded `ThirdParty/Fonts/NanumGothic-Regular.ttf`.\n  - `Display` is {Baskerville, Georgia, Times New Roman, Noto Serif}, and WebGL uses Body.\n  - Noto Serif KR and Cinzel are not bundled (plan D6).\n  - `check_ui_contract.py:61-62` rejects creating fonts outside `UiTheme.cs`.\n- **Shadow and outline** are Unity `Shadow`/`Outline` with hard offsets only: `P/ItemDetailView.Style.cs:140`, `P/GlobalHudView.cs:207`, `P/AttendanceWindow.cs:182`, `P/TitleScreenView.cs:39`, `Outline` at `P/GameUI.Plaza.cs:106`. Rich text is `<color=#hex>` in 6 places (e.g. `P/EquipmentComparisonView.cs:19`); there is no `<size>` or `<b>`.\n- **Gradient-filled text** does not exist anywhere.\n- **Line height and wrapping.**\n  - `Text.lineSpacing` is a multiplier of the font's own line height (set to 1 or 1.12: `P/ItemDetailView.Style.cs:30`, `P/StorageWindow.cs:469`). There is no CSS px line-height.\n  - No keep-all control exists. A grep for NBSP, ZWSP and word-joiner characters across `Runtime` finds nothing.\n  - Wrapping is only checked via `cachedTextGenerator.lineCount` and `preferredHeight` in smokes (`P/RuntimeJewelerSmoke.cs:57-58`).\n  - `resizeTextForBestFit` is the usual overflow fix (`P/BlacksmithWindow.Controls.cs:25`).\n- **Measurement helpers** that could replace the HTML's `tw()`/`fitFs()` (`D/SkillWindow.dc.html:486-497`):\n  - `Text.preferredWidth/Height` (`P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:111`, `P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:105`).\n  - Throwaway-Text `TextWidth(value,size,bold,serif)` and `TextHeight(value,w,size,bold)` (`P/BlacksmithWindow.Chrome.cs:41-51`).\n  - Static, no GameObject: `t.cachedTextGeneratorForLayout.GetPreferredWidth(value,t.GetGenerationSettings(Vector2.zero))/t.pixelsPerUnit` (`P/GameUI.Rift.cs:70-71`).\n  - `new TextGenerator().GetPreferredWidth(value,new TextGenerationSettings{font=UiFonts.Body,fontSize=size,fontStyle=FontStyle.Normal,scaleFactor=1,richText=true})` (`P/MonsterCodexWindow.cs:129`).\n  - Set `Canvas.scaleFactor` before measuring on a first render (`P/ContentWindowView.cs:39-40`).\n\n## 5. ANIMATION\n\nThere is no tween library. Everything is `Update` or a coroutine on `Time.unscaledTime` or `unscaledDeltaTime`, because pause is `RunState.paused`, not `timeScale`.\n\n- **`UiButtonFace`** (`P/UiButtonFace.cs:21,39,43-49`): a state change sets progress to 0, and `Update` lerps the palette and calls `SetVerticesDirty` each step. `Show` early-outs when nothing changed (:30-31), so a repeated Repaint does not restart it.\n- **`ForgeWorkingPulse`** (`P/BlacksmithWindow.Slots.cs:245-250`): a CanvasGroup alpha of `.65+.35*cos(unscaledTime*2π/1.5)`, with no mesh rebuild. It reads PlayerPrefs each frame.\n- **`TutorialAnchorRing`** (`P/TutorialAnchorRing.cs:17-36`): `Update()=>SetVerticesDirty()` every frame. It has a breathing border, ripple and bobbing pointer, and is still under reduce-motion (:20).\n- **`AttendanceClaimGlow`** is a static mesh.\n- **`ContentDockView`** (`P/GameUI.ContentDock.cs:73-112`): `Seconds=.22f`, step = `Time.unscaledDeltaTime/Seconds`, with a `Settled` early-out and `Snap(bool)`.\n- **Window tickers:**\n  - `RuneMasterWindow.TickFusion` (`P/RuneMasterWindow.cs:173-184`): start time, `SmoothStep`, `Lerp`.\n  - `RiftRewardRevealMotion` (`P/RiftRewardRevealWindow.cs:42-47`): scale .86 to 1 plus alpha.\n  - `DialogueEntrance` (`P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:44-51`).\n  - Blacksmith's 0.25 s ticker (`P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:43-49`).\n- **Cheap alpha:** `canvasRenderer.SetAlpha` (`P/UiButton.cs:63,68`) and CanvasGroup do not rebuild meshes.\n- **Reduce motion:** `WorldLighting.ReduceMotionKey=\"hellscript.reduce-motion\"` (`P/WorldLighting.cs:46`) is a PlayerPrefs int. `StoryDialogueWindow.ReduceMotion` is that flag OR `SystemReduceMotion` (`P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:55`).\n  - The OS flag is read only on macOS via objc, cached 1 s (:57-70), and is `false` elsewhere (:72).\n  - No settings UI writes the key (comment `P/WorldLighting.cs:44-45`), and `ForgeWorkingPulse` ignores the OS flag.\n- **Pooled floating numbers:** no UI one exists. The nearest pools are the `StatusStripView` entries (`P/StatusStripView.cs:21,75-77`), `PrologueGate` `DimPool=16` (`P/PrologueGate.cs:16,31`), and the capped, oldest-recycled 3D `WorldFx` transients (`P/WorldFx.cs:13-31`).\n\n## 6. SMOKE AND SCREENSHOT FRAMEWORK\n\n- **Structure.**\n  - A smoke is a `MonoBehaviour` in `P/Runtime*Smoke*.cs`, wrapped in `#if UNITY_EDITOR || DEVELOPMENT_BUILD`.\n  - A `[RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod(AfterSceneLoad)] static void Boot()` returns unless `Debug.isDebugBuild` and the flag is in `GetCommandLineArgs()`. It sets `Application.runInBackground=true` and creates the GameObject (`P/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:42-47`, `P/RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke.cs:210-217`).\n  - `P/RuntimeBlacksmithSmoke.cs:20-26` also sets `InputSystem.settings.backgroundBehavior=IgnoreFocus`.\n  - `Start()` is a coroutine. It reads `-hellscriptSavePath` (required) and `-hellscriptScreenshots`, `-hellscriptEvidence` or `-hellscriptEvidencePath` (`P/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:106-109`; the three names vary per smoke). It then waits 1 s and calls `FindAnyObjectByType<GameController>()`.\n  - Failures: an exception writes `failure.txt` and calls `Quit(1)` (:48-51). Success writes `runtime.txt` or an `..._OK` marker such as `HELLSCRIPT_BATTLEQUICK_SMOKE_OK` (`P/RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke.cs:343-344`).\n  - Files starting `Runtime` and containing `Smoke` are skipped by both UI check tools (`check_ui_contract.py:52`, `check_ui_refresh.py:51`) and by `LocalizationTests` (`T/LocalizationTests.cs:259`).\n- **Helpers** (copied per smoke, not shared):\n  - `Require(bool,string)`.\n  - `Find(name)` (:52).\n  - `Bounds(RectTransform)`.\n  - `Tap(name)` scrolls the button's ScrollRect to centre, then calls `TapAt` (:54-65).\n  - `TapAt(Vector2,name)` calls `EventSystem.current.RaycastAll`, requires the first hit to be the button, then runs `ExecuteEvents.Execute` for pointerDown, pointerUp and pointerClick (:71-81).\n  - `Hold(target,seconds)` (BattleQuick :29-33).\n  - Waits: `yield return null` twice, or `WaitForSecondsRealtime(.25f)` plus `Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases()`.\n  - `Resize(w,h,lang)` (:82-87): `game.ApplyLanguage(lang); game.UI.RefreshCanvasLayout(); Screen.SetResolution(w,h,Windowed)`, poll up to 8 s, then 0.4 s.\n  - `Capture(name)` (:88-89): `Debug.developerConsoleVisible=false; Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases(); WaitForEndOfFrame; ScreenCapture.CaptureScreenshotAsTexture()`, then `EncodeToPNG` and `File.WriteAllBytes`. RuneBoard uses `CaptureScreenshot(path)` (`P/RuntimeRuneBoardSmoke.cs:40`).\n  - Real mouse device: `InputSystem.AddDevice<Mouse>` (`P/RuntimeRuneBoardSmoke.cs:94`).\n  - Notch: `UiSafeArea.Simulate(left,bottom,right,top)` (debug builds only, `P/UiSafeArea.cs:59-61`) and `StopSimulating()`. The plan's iPhone insets are already used at `P/RuntimeScreenSettingsSmoke.RiftTitle.cs:69` (956 wide: 62/21/62/0; 440 wide: 0/34/0/62).\n  - `UiSafeArea.AspectRatio=0` resets the aspect frame (`P/RuntimeRuneBoardSmoke.cs:45`).\n  - Resume: a second launch with the same save path and `-hellscriptSkillTreeResume` asserts persisted state, writes `restart.txt` and quits (:118-125).\n- **Exact commands** (clone with `cp -Rc Assets Packages ProjectSettings Library <work>/proj; rm -f <work>/proj/Temp/UnityLockfile`; Unity 6000.6.0f1). `-nographics` and `-logFile` are from `CPU_Optimization_20261002.md:120`; the Unity binary path is from `R/tools/hunyuan_monster_install.py:31`.\n```\n/Applications/Unity/Hub/Editor/6000.6.0f1/Unity.app/Contents/MacOS/Unity -batchmode -nographics -quit -projectPath <work>/proj -buildTarget StandaloneOSX -executeMethod Hellscript.Editor.ProjectBuilder.BuildMac -hellscriptBuildOutput <out>/HELLSCRIPT.app -logFile <out>/build.log\nARGS=(-hellscriptSkillTreeD4Smoke -hellscriptOfflineQa -hellscriptSavePath \"$SAVE\" -hellscriptScreenshots \"$SHOTS\" -screen-fullscreen 0 -screen-width 440 -screen-height 956); <out>/HELLSCRIPT.app/Contents/MacOS/HELLSCRIPT \"${ARGS[@]}\"\n```\n  `BuildMac` is a development build (`E/ProjectBuilder.cs:68-71,78-95`) and the output must end in `.app` (:110-121). Use bash arrays; zsh does not split words. `-hellscriptOfflineQa` is only needed for flows that start at the title.\n- **What the docs say.**\n  - No \"Smoke build recipe\" heading exists. `R/Docs/Design/Hunt_Edict_UI_Overhaul.en.md:577-582` (§12.6) says AGENTS.md has none and lists the steps used locally.\n  - Command lines are in `Docs/Implementation/Map_Display_Option.md:134-138`, `Town_Hunyuan_Models.md:109` and `Blacksmith_Validation.md:149`. Plan §15 is `D4_Skill_Tree_Plan_20261012.md:506` and the smoke spec is :460-471.\n  - No script automates smokes. The only runner in the repo is `R/tools/profile_native_cpu.py` (CPU profile). The `run_smokes.py` named in that doc is not in the repo.\n\n## 7. EDITMODE UI TESTS\n\n- **Building uGUI in EditMode.**\n  - Create `new GameObject(\"x\",typeof(RectTransform),typeof(Canvas))`, add an `EventSystem` child for pointer tests (`T/UiButtonTests.cs:13-20`, `T/StoreViewBindingTests.cs:19-31`), or make a `ContentWindowHost` root, then call the real `Open(...)` (`T/SharedUiTests.cs:63`, `T/MonsterCodexWindowTests.cs:14-23`).\n  - Measure `RectTransform.rect`, `Text.preferredHeight` and `Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases()`.\n  - Vary layout by `UiSafeArea.AspectRatio=w/(float)h` (the frame is fitted inside the Game view, `P/UiSafeArea.cs:25-26`).\n  - `T/MonsterCodexWindowTests.cs:43-62` is the pattern: five sizes by ko/en, asserting row counts, tap targets >= 44 px, `preferredHeight<=rect.height+.5` and `Loc.MissingCount==0`. English comes from `Loc.Use(\"en\",LocalizationTable.Parse(Resources.Load<TextAsset>(\"Localization/en\").text).Entries)`. TearDown resets `AspectRatio=0`, `StopSimulating()` and `Loc.UseSource()`.\n  - `TouchLayoutTests` is pure maths on `Runtime/Core/TouchLayout.cs`, with no GameObjects.\n  - Pure-layout precedent: `BattleHudLayout`/`InventoryLayout` with `[TestCaseSource]` (`T/BattleHudLayoutTests.cs:9-26`), a good template for the plan's layout function.\n  - `T/GraphicComponentTests.cs:13-24` reflects over every `Graphic` subclass: each needs `[RequireComponent(typeof(CanvasRenderer))]`, and `AddComponent(type)` with no setup must not throw.\n- **Mesh golden and allocation test:** `T/ForgePresentationAllocationTests.cs:13-24,54-68` reflects `OnPopulateMesh` into a delegate and compares `vertices`, `colors32` and `triangles` with `T/Fixtures/forge-ring-baseline-N.json`. It then asserts `Is.Not.AllocatingGCMemory()` after warm-up.\n- **Loading repo files.**\n  - `File.ReadAllText(Path.Combine(Application.dataPath,\"..\",\"Docs/Design/MonsterRoster/roster.json\"))` (`T/MonsterSoakTests.cs:16`).\n  - CWD-relative `File.ReadAllText(\"Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Fixtures/RuneNativeParity.json\")` with `JsonUtility` and `[Serializable]` classes (`T/RuneBoardNativeTests.cs:18`). This is a JS-to-C# parity fixture.\n  - `Path.Combine(Application.dataPath,\"HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Fixtures/RuneV13Layout.json\")` (`T/RuneV13Tests.cs:67`).\n  - There is no `InternalsVisibleTo`, so tests see only public members or use `BindingFlags.NonPublic` reflection (`T/StoreViewBindingTests.cs:18`).\n\n## 8. ICONS AND MASKS\n\n- **Crop.** A circular crop is a `Plate` `Image` with sprite `Art/GlobalHUD/mask-circle` and a stencil `Mask` (`showMaskGraphic=true`). The child `Icon` is an `Image` with `preserveAspect=true` (`P/SkillIconView.cs:28-35,41-46`). Passives use `mask-square` and `frame-active`. The HUD seal uses the same approach with `showMaskGraphic=false` (`P/GlobalHudView.cs:178-183`).\n- **Masks.** They are 256² white RGBA sprites, bilinear. `mask-square` is a rounded square and `mask-circle` is a circle. A frame image (`frame-seal`, `frame-active`) covers the hard stencil edge.\n- **Skill icons.** `Resources/Art/ClassSkillIcons/{Warrior,Ranger,Mage}/<id>.png`: 37 each, 1254², no mipmaps, not readable.\n- **Budget rows.** `E/ResourceTextureBudget.cs:24` is Android 512 ASTC_6x6. The desktop table (`:63-82`, `Art/ClassSkillIcons/` 512) gives Standalone BC7 and WebGL ETC2_RGBA8. `Art/SkillTree/` has its own rows (`tree-backdrop` 1024, rest 512). Masks and frames have no row.\n- **Tests.** `T/BuildResourceTests.cs:11-32` checks one icon sample for overrides plus GUID/meta stability; `P/RuntimeBuildResourceSmoke.cs:20-27` samples at runtime.\n- **Old tree art** (`Art/SkillTree/node-frame-*`, `tree-backdrop`, `skill-point-gem`) is used at `P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:25,77,86,232-241`.\n- **New ids.** The 84 modifier ids are unknown to `TryResolve`. Extend it, or `Resources.Load` the sprite and call `SetSprite`.\n\n## 9. FILE/ASSEMBLY CONVENTIONS\n\n- **Layout.**\n  - `P/` is flat (493 `.cs` files, 157 of them smokes). Namespace is `Hellscript`.\n  - There are three asmdefs: `Runtime/Hellscript.Runtime.asmdef` (all of Core, Presentation and Runes), `Editor/Hellscript.Editor.asmdef`, and `Tests/Editor/Hellscript.Tests.asmdef` (Editor only).\n  - Partial naming is `X.cs` (Open, Update, Reflow) plus `X.<Topic>.cs`, as in `BlacksmithWindow.Chrome/Controls/Slots.cs` and `HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs`. Use `SkillTreeD4Window*.cs` and `RuntimeSkillTreeD4Smoke*.cs`.\n- **Registration in GameUI.** Add a partial `GameUI.<Name>.cs`:\n  - Follow `P/GameUI.Blacksmith.cs:5-21`, `GameUI.RuneBoard.cs` and `GameUI.AspectStone.cs`: field, public accessor for smokes, `Show…()` and `Close…()`.\n  - `Show…()` gates with `RequireContent(...)`, closes sibling windows (`CloseRuneMaster();CloseBlacksmith();CloseHudPanel();CloseStorage();CloseEquipmentShop();ResetTownInput();game.Town.Cancel()`), then calls `Open(transform,…)` with a `closed` callback that nulls the field and runs `RefreshHud();RefreshPlaza();`.\n  - The host is created at `P/GameUI.cs:38`.\n  - `CommonPanelOpen` (`P/GameUI.ScreenSettings.cs:22`) picks up `windowHost.BlocksGameplay` automatically.\n  - Language: add to the `P/GameUI.cs:109` chain, or poll in `Update`.\n  - Entry points to repoint: `P/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:69`, `P/GameUI.FirstPlay.cs:22`, `P/HuntEdictWindow.SkillPresets.cs:59`, `P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:60`, `P/RiftEntryWindow.cs:355`.\n- **Template.** `R/tools/new_content_ui.py` plus `R/tools/templates/ContentWindow.cs.txt` emits a static `<Name>Window` that calls `ContentWindowView.Open`. That is the route that needs no ADAPTERS entry.\n- **`check_ui_contract.py` failures** (`R/tools/check_ui_contract.py`):\n  - `{owner}: missing shared owner {token}` (:58).\n  - `{name}: use UiFonts instead of creating a font` (:62).\n  - `{name}: new content must open ContentWindowView; specialized layouts require a reviewed adapter` (:67): any `class \\w+Window` whose owner is not in ADAPTERS and has no `ContentWindowView.Open`.\n  - `{name}: canvas ownership belongs to ContentWindowView/ContentWindowHost` (:70): `AddComponent<Canvas>` or `typeof(Canvas)` outside ADAPTERS or `CANVAS_OWNERS` (:25-26).\n  - `{name}: chrome colour {hex} must use a UiTheme token` (:77): any `\"rrggbb\"` or `\"rrggbbaa\"` string literal that `chrome_colour()` (:33-42) judges warm, dark or ivory. By that function, `b9c6d0`, `fff3d6` and `d3af72` fail, while `6f8291` and `e07a32` pass. The rule is heuristic, so put every design colour in `UiTheme.cs` (exempt, :31).\n  - `reusable views cannot mutate or read a live account` for `PURE_VIEWS` (:78-79).\n  - `test_ui_contract.py:22` runs the same check on a copy of the whole Presentation folder.\n- **`check_ui_refresh.py:55-66`:** `{path}:{line}: define visibleState or an audited owner guard`. Every `StoreViewBinding.Attach` in a top-level `P/*.cs` needs >= 5 arguments or `visibleState:`. It scans only top-level files and skips `Runtime*`.\n- **Source-scanning EditMode tests.**\n  - `T/LocalizationTests.cs:239-255`: every non-interpolated Korean literal in Runtime (smokes excluded) needs an exact `en.txt` entry, and interpolated Korean fails.\n  - `T/EditorNullPatternTests.cs:41-49`: no `GetComponent…() ??` or `?.`; use `TryGetComponent`.\n  - `T/GraphicComponentTests.cs` (see section 7).\n- **Docs.** `Shared_UI_Contract(.en).md` has a section per adapter; :108 is the old skill-tree adapter. `AgentRules/Shared_UI.md:12` requires the exception's reason and verification to be written down.\n\n## RISKS\n\n1. **Font.** Legacy `Text` has an int `fontSize`, so the design's 10.5, 12.5 and 14.5 pt sizes round. Noto Serif KR and Cinzel are not available, and `UiFonts.Display` varies by OS. Line-height is a font-metric multiplier, and there is no letter-spacing or keep-all. Gradient title text and glow need new code.\n2. **No anti-aliasing on custom meshes.** Only `HuntEdictSurface` has a feather fringe. Hex, arc and round shapes will look jagged without one. `UiMesh` also lacks hairline snapping except where `px=1/canvas.scaleFactor` is copied (`P/UiButtonFace.cs:55-56`).\n3. **Colour space.** `ProjectSettings.asset:49` is Linear (`m_ActiveColorSpace: 1`). Alpha compositing and gradients can differ from CSS gamma blending, and nothing in the repo verifies this.\n4. **Filters.**\n   - Blur, grayscale, brightness and soft drop-shadow have no engine path. A new shader needs Stencil and `_ClipRect` support, which `PuzzleHubTone` lacks.\n   - Skill icons are non-readable and have no mips, so baked blur is impossible, and plan §16 forbids touching icons.\n5. **Clipping.** `RectMask2D` plates clip outer glows and the design's out-of-box ornaments (`gx-pan-*` at `top:-12px`). These need an unclipped layer above the scroll.\n6. **Performance.**\n   - `UiMesh` helpers allocate, so any per-frame rebuild (ignite, glint, ring bloom) needs allocation-free dedicated Graphics.\n   - Per-icon stencil `Mask` (`SkillIconView`) breaks batching across about 48 icons.\n   - Moving scroll content re-batches the whole canvas.\n   - `AGENTS.md` and `CPU_Performance.md` forbid steady per-frame work.\n7. **Scale mismatch.** `UiTheme.Scale` bases are 800x450 and 405x720, and the Blacksmith U is clamped 8-17. The design is 1:1 px (440x860, 832x419, 1152x648 stages), so a new fit-and-centre scale is needed. `UiTheme.Scale` must still be called somewhere real (not in a comment) to satisfy the ADAPTERS token.\n8. **Scroll.** No two-axis or X-persisting scroll exists. Nested scroll is avoided by locking the outer one. The landscape plate's right-edge fade has a precedent only in `GlobalHudFade.shader` (`P/StatusStripView.cs:46`).\n9. **Reduce motion.** No toggle writes the key, the OS flag is macOS only, and `ForgeWorkingPulse` ignores it. Use `StoryDialogueWindow.ReduceMotion`.\n10. **Screenshot comparison.** References are 2x (880x1912, 1912x880, 2880x1620). `macRetinaSupport:1` and `resizableWindow:0` (`ProjectSettings.asset:89,104`) mean oversized windows may be clamped. A capture strategy is needed; nothing in the repo automates smokes or the side-by-side comparison.\n11. **Mask radius.** `mask-square` radius is fixed (about 13%) while the design's radii differ per widget. The stencil edge is hard. A UV-mesh crop (gap 9) is the alternative.\n12. **Texture weight.** 92 new 512² icons are about 24 MB each for BC7 (desktop) and ETC2 (WebGL), not the 11 MB APK-only figure in plan §11.\n13. **Gating and lint.**\n    - `SkillIconAssets` does not resolve new ids.\n    - A localization entry is needed for every Korean literal.\n    - New colours must be `UiTheme` tokens (the lint is heuristic).\n    - `GetComponent … ?.` is banned.\n    - Pre-existing worktree edits and the uncommitted `D/golden/` mean tests reading goldens depend on commit state.", "html": "<p>Read-only pass done; nothing was changed. No <code>SkillTreeD4*<\/code> code exists yet. Paths are abbreviated:<\/p><ul><li><code>R<\/code> = <code>/Users/t8g-2410-pn-005/Documents/MyProject/HELLSCRIPT/wt-d4-skill-plan<\/code><\/li><li><code>P<\/code> = <code>R/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation<\/code><\/li><li><code>T<\/code> = <code>R/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Editor<\/code><\/li><li><code>E<\/code> = <code>R/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Editor<\/code><\/li><li><code>D<\/code> = <code>R/Docs/Design/D4SkillTree<\/code><\/li><\/ul><p>The worktree already has someone else&#x27;s uncommitted edits: <code>D/extract.js<\/code> and <code>D/skill_tree_d4.json<\/code> are modified, and <code>D/golden/<\/code> is untracked (layout, viewmodel, anatomy and interaction JSON, <code>styles.json<\/code>, <code>fx.json<\/code>).<\/p><h2 id=\"1-drawing-primitives\">1. DRAWING PRIMITIVES<\/h2><p><strong>API (Graphic local space, y up, unless noted)<\/strong><\/p><ul><li><strong><code>UiMesh<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/UiButtonFace.cs:156-256<\/code>) is a static class writing into a <code>VertexHelper<\/code>, so it needs a <code>MaskableGraphic<\/code> host.<\/li><li><code>Inset(Rect,n)<\/code>, <code>Box(m,Rect,upper,lower)<\/code>, <code>Frame(m,Rect,n,c)<\/code><\/li><li><code>RoundedBox(m,Rect,radius,upper,lower)<\/code>, <code>RoundedRing(m,Rect,radius,width,ink)<\/code><\/li><li><code>Gradient(m,Rect,cut,Func&lt;float,Color&gt;,bands=6)<\/code> fills a chamfered rect with colour = f(y).<\/li><li><code>Ring(m,Rect,cut,width,c)<\/code> is a chamfered outline.<\/li><li><code>Diamond(m,Vector2,radius,c)<\/code>, <code>Brackets(m,Rect,n,arm,c)<\/code><\/li><li>Rounded shapes use a fixed 24-point contour (<code>RoundedContour<\/code> :174) with no AA. <code>RoundedContour<\/code>, <code>Gradient<\/code> and <code>Brackets<\/code> allocate arrays or Lists on every call.<\/li><li><strong><code>UiButtonFace : MaskableGraphic<\/code><\/strong> (:10) is added by <code>UiButton.Configure(role,chosen,locked)<\/code> (<code>P/UiButton.cs:28-42<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>Show(role,chosen,locked,available,hovered,pressed,focused,instant)<\/code> (:27) is a no-op when nothing changed. <code>SetChrome(Gilt|Minimal)<\/code>.<\/li><li>It draws a chamfered gradient face, hairline ring, top light, rising glow, and for Primary a double line plus lozenges.<\/li><li>The Tab role is a gradient strip, bottom bar, gold bar and diamond (:84-98). Minimal chrome uses <code>RoundedBox/RoundedRing<\/code> with radius &lt;= 5 (:127-142).<\/li><li>The fade is <code>Time.unscaledDeltaTime/UiTheme.ButtonFade<\/code> (.085 s) (:43-49).<\/li><li><strong><code>UiTheme<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/UiTheme.cs:8-130<\/code>):<\/li><li>Hex consts at :12-21 (Void, Background, Inset, Panel, Raised, Hover, Selected, Border, Edge, GoldDeep, Gold, GoldBright, Text, Muted, Faint, Success, Danger, Primary). Matching <code>Color<\/code> properties come from <code>StorageSurface.Hex<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Tint(hex,alpha)<\/code> :44, <code>Title/Heading/Body/Caption = 20/15/12/10<\/code> :50, <code>Scale(Rect)<\/code> :54.<\/li><li><code>ButtonPalette(role,chosen,locked,available,hover,pressed)<\/code> returns <code>UiButtonPalette{top,bottom,edge,light,accent,glow}<\/code> (:80; struct at <code>P/UiButtonFace.cs:149<\/code>). <code>MinimalButtonPalette<\/code> :115. <code>Button/Choice/Skin/Backdrop<\/code>.<\/li><li>There are no steel, ember, line-state or rim-gradient tokens.<\/li><li><strong><code>UiLayout<\/code><\/strong> (:148-163):<\/li><li><code>Rect(name,parent)<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Place(r,x,y,w,h)<\/code>: top-left anchor and pivot, y down, size &gt;= 1.<\/li><li><code>Stretch(r)<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Text(parent,name,value,x,y,w,h,int size,Color,Font font=null)<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Clear(parent)<\/code>: SetActive(false) plus Destroy.<\/li><li><strong><code>UiWindowFrame : Image<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/UiWindowFrame.cs:9<\/code>; fields <code>header, footer, corners<\/code>) draws a gradient panel, header band, border and gilt <code>Brackets<\/code> (no dots). <code>Divider(m,x0,x1,y,n,c,strength,jewel,hole)<\/code> (:39) fades its ends and has a centre diamond. <code>UiHeaderRule.Attach(Transform header)<\/code> :61.<\/li><li><strong><code>UiIconButton<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/UiIconButton.cs:11<\/code>) has <code>Create(parent,name,icon,x,y,w,h,Action click,framed=true,Color? tint=null,bool backdrop=false,string folder=null,Rect? uv=null)<\/code> (:15) and <code>CreateGlyph(...)<\/code> (:23). Both return a <code>UiButton<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong><code>SkillIconView<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/SkillIconView.cs:10<\/code>):<\/li><li><code>Create(parent,passive)<\/code> :18, <code>SetKind<\/code>, <code>SetSkill(id,squareFrame=false)<\/code> :48, <code>SetSprite<\/code>.<\/li><li>Children are Plate (an <code>Image<\/code> with a stencil <code>Mask<\/code>), Icon, Cover (Radial360 cooldown) and Frame.<\/li><li><code>SkillIconAssets.TryResolve(id,out passive,out sprite)<\/code> (:57) only knows ids that <code>ClassSkills.Find<\/code> returns, plus legacy atlas ids.<\/li><li><strong><code>SkillTreeGraphic<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/SkillTreeGraphic.cs:25<\/code>):<\/li><li>Builder API: <code>Create(parent,name,x,y,w,h)<\/code> :32, <code>Bind(UiButton)<\/code>, <code>Line(a,b,width,c,hot)<\/code>, <code>Disc<\/code>, <code>Ring<\/code>, <code>Glow(center,inner,outer,c)<\/code> (radial halo), <code>Diamond<\/code>, <code>DiamondRing<\/code>, <code>Box(x,y,w,h,top,bottom)<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Link(a,b,crossing,width,c)<\/code> is orthogonal, three segments only.<\/li><li>Coordinates are top-left px, and the whole shape list is re-emitted on every dirty.<\/li><li>A private <code>Polygon(...,sides,start)<\/code> (:98) exists. <code>SkillTreeLayout<\/code> :13 is the legacy 37-node placement.<\/li><li><strong><code>HuntEdictSurface : Image<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/HuntEdictSurface.cs:9<\/code>): <code>Paint(skin)<\/code> :16 (named skins :20-62); public <code>fill, edge, radius, edgeWidth, underline<\/code>. It draws a rounded fill, ring and 1 px AA feather (:80-84). <code>radius=100<\/code> gives a pill.<\/li><li><strong><code>StorageSurface : Image<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/StorageSurface.cs:8<\/code>): <code>top,bottom,edge,bottomOnly,sidesOnly,dashed,inset<\/code>, <code>Paint(upper,lower,border)<\/code>, <code>Hex(string)<\/code>. Square corners and a 1 px edge. Dashes are a fixed 3/3 px on straight edges (:37-46).<\/li><li><strong>Others:<\/strong><\/li><li><code>StorageGlyph<\/code>: 24-unit line icons by <code>symbol<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>UIRectBorder<\/code> (BaseMeshEffect), <code>UiLockGraphic<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>AttendanceClaimGlow<\/code>: static radial glow plus 6 rays.<\/li><li><code>TutorialAnchorRing<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>EquipmentRevealGraphic<\/code>: Frame = L corners plus diamond dots (:16-29).<\/li><li><code>TitleFrameGraphic/TitleOrnament<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>RuneGemMesh<\/code> (<code>mainTexture<\/code> override :12, rune atlas): public <code>Hex/Circle/Quad/Line/Outline(points,width,color,dashed)/Polygon(points,light,dark)<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>TownCircleGraphic<\/code> (<code>P/TownJoystick.cs:52<\/code>), <code>ForgeMilestoneRing<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>SelectionRune<\/code> and <code>SelectionGroundShadow<\/code> (<code>P/CharacterSelectionStage.cs:95,106<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>VignetteGraphic<\/code> (<code>P/TutorialCinematic.cs:181<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>TrainingDpsChart<\/code>: polyline plus private dashed/dot helpers (:49,:54).<\/li><li><code>DialogueReveal : BaseMeshEffect<\/code> (<code>P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:243<\/code>).<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Feature support<\/strong><\/p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Feature<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Closest existing<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Verdict<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Vertical gradient fill<\/td><td><code>UiMesh.Box/Gradient/RoundedBox<\/code>, <code>StorageSurface.top/bottom<\/code><\/td><td>yes<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Gradient (gilt) border<\/td><td>every ring is single colour; <code>Divider<\/code> fades alpha only<\/td><td>no<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Rounded rect, per-widget radius<\/td><td><code>RoundedBox/RoundedRing(radius)<\/code>, <code>HuntEdictSurface.radius<\/code><\/td><td>yes (one radius for all corners; AA only in HuntEdictSurface)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Dashed outline<\/td><td><code>StorageSurface.dashed<\/code><\/td><td>partly (straight edges, 1 px, fixed 3/3)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Dashed line<\/td><td><code>RuneGemMesh.Outline(dashed)<\/code> (4.5/7.3), <code>TrainingDpsChart.Dashed<\/code> (private)<\/td><td>partly<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Hexagon medallion<\/td><td><code>SkillTreeGraphic.Polygon<\/code> and <code>RuneBoardGraphic.Hex<\/code> are private; <code>RuneGemMesh.Hex<\/code> is atlas-bound<\/td><td>no (no usable public one)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Segmented arc / conic ring<\/td><td>none<\/td><td>no<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Soft outer glow / box-shadow<\/td><td><code>SkillTreeGraphic.Glow<\/code> (circular), <code>AttendanceClaimGlow<\/code>, 1 px feather<\/td><td>partly<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Inner shadow<\/td><td><code>StorageSurface.inset<\/code> (hard 1 px), <code>UiButtonFace<\/code> top light<\/td><td>partly<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Blurred backdrop art<\/td><td>no blur code or shader<\/td><td>no<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Polyline with glow under-stroke<\/td><td><code>Line/Link<\/code>; the two-pass wide-translucent plus narrow stroke is at <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:52<\/code><\/td><td>partly (orthogonal only, no joins or caps)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Corner ornaments (L plus dots)<\/td><td><code>UiMesh.Brackets<\/code>, <code>EquipmentRevealGraphic.Frame<\/code><\/td><td>partly<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Gradient text / text shadow<\/td><td>Unity <code>Shadow<\/code>/<code>Outline<\/code><\/td><td>no / yes (hard offset)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Circle / square crops<\/td><td><code>SkillIconView<\/code><\/td><td>yes (fixed radius, hard stencil edge)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Scroll plate and panel body<\/td><td>see section 3<\/td><td>yes, single axis only<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Tab buttons<\/td><td><code>UiButtonRole.Tab<\/code><\/td><td>partly (gold, not ember)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>One-shot FX<\/td><td>see section 5<\/td><td>partly<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p><strong>GAPS and the idiomatic way to fill each<\/strong><\/p><ol><li><strong>Gradient rims<\/strong> (<code>GILT_RIM<\/code> and <code>STEEL_RIM<\/code> are 5-stop vertical gradients): add a <code>RoundedRing(..., Func&lt;float,Color&gt; byY)<\/code> overload to <code>UiMesh<\/code>, mirroring <code>Gradient<\/code>. Put the stop arrays in <code>UiTheme<\/code>, which is exempt from the colour lint.<\/li><li><strong>Hex, conic arc, angular gradient<\/strong>:<\/li><li>The design&#x27;s HEX is a regular pointy-top hexagon, so <code>Polygon(…,6,90)<\/code> already draws it.<\/li><li>Add <code>UiMesh.Hex<\/code>/<code>HexRing<\/code> and <code>UiMesh.Arc(m,center,rIn,rOut,startDeg,sweepDeg,Func&lt;float,Color&gt; byAngle,segments)<\/code>.<\/li><li>Expose them as new <code>Kind<\/code>s in <code>SkillTreeGraphic<\/code> (builder style).<\/li><li><strong>Polyline with joins, round caps, dash, glow under-stroke, partial range<\/strong> (ignite and glint): add a new <code>PolylineGraphic : MaskableGraphic<\/code> per state colour, as plan 9.7 says. Give it <code>SetRange(t0,t1)<\/code> and preallocated buffers; reuse the dash maths of <code>RuneGemMesh.Outline<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Rounded dashed outline<\/strong>: add <code>UiMesh.DashedRing<\/code> walking the <code>RoundedContour<\/code> perimeter.<\/li><li><strong>Box-shadow, inner shadow, radial plate gradients<\/strong>:<\/li><li>Add <code>UiMesh.Glow/Inner(m,Rect,radius,spread,Color)<\/code>: a ring from the inflated contour to the rect with an alpha ramp, generalising the feather at <code>P/HuntEdictSurface.cs:80-84<\/code>.<\/li><li>For radial fills, use ellipse fans like <code>SelectionGroundShadow<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>RectMask2D<\/code> clips glows at the plate edge.<\/li><li><strong>Blur and CSS filters<\/strong> (blur 14-18 px art, grayscale/brightness on locked icons):<\/li><li>Add one UI shader under <code>Resources/<\/code>, modelled on <code>Resources/GlobalHudFade.shader<\/code>. It has Stencil and <code>_ClipRect<\/code>, so it works under <code>Mask<\/code>/<code>RectMask2D<\/code>.<\/li><li>Fold in <code>_Tone<\/code> (brightness, saturation) from <code>Resources/Art/PuzzleHubTone.shader<\/code>. That shader has no stencil or clip, so it must not be used inside a scroll plate.<\/li><li>Own the <code>new Material(shader)<\/code> per window and destroy it (<code>P/PuzzleHubWindow.cs:37,223<\/code>).<\/li><li>Icons are 1254², <code>isReadable:0<\/code>, no mips (<code>W01.png.meta<\/code>), so CPU or baked blur is out, and plan §16 forbids resizing icons.<\/li><li><strong>Gradient text<\/strong>: add a <code>TextGradient : BaseMeshEffect<\/code>. <code>DialogueReveal.Conceal<\/code> (<code>P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:243-261<\/code>) already rewrites per-glyph vertex colours. Add it before <code>Shadow<\/code> so the shadow copies stay black. Soft text glow is only possible by approximation (<code>Outline<\/code> or several <code>Shadow<\/code>s).<\/li><li><strong>Dotted corner ornaments and centre diamond rule<\/strong>: compose <code>Brackets<\/code> + <code>Diamond<\/code> + a new <code>UiMesh.Disc<\/code>. Draw them on a layer above the scroll mask, because the design draws them outside the clip.<\/li><li><strong>Icon crops with exact radius and dim/desaturate<\/strong>:<\/li><li><code>mask-square<\/code> has a fixed radius of about 13%, decoded from its alpha.<\/li><li>Add a textured rounded-rect <code>MaskableGraphic<\/code> with UVs, like the <code>RuneGemMesh.mainTexture<\/code> pattern. This avoids a stencil <code>Mask<\/code> per icon.<\/li><li><strong>FX<\/strong>: build them from items 2 and 3 plus <code>CanvasGroup<\/code>/<code>canvasRenderer.SetAlpha<\/code>, <code>localScale<\/code>, a skewed quad inside <code>RectMask2D<\/code> for the shine, and a small pool of <code>Text<\/code> for &quot;+1&quot;.<\/li><\/ol><h2 id=\"2-custom-unit-adapter-windows\">2. CUSTOM-UNIT ADAPTER WINDOWS<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Unit.<\/strong> <code>BlacksmithWindow.Reflow<\/code> (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:61-72<\/code>):<\/li><li><code>safe=UiSafeArea.Current<\/code>, <code>landscape=safe.width&gt;safe.height<\/code>, <code>scale=UiTheme.Scale(safe)<\/code>. That formula is min(w/800,h/450) landscape and min(w/405,h/720) portrait (<code>P/UiTheme.cs:54<\/code>).<\/li><li>Canvas units are <code>width=safe.width/scale<\/code> and <code>height=safe.height/scale<\/code>.<\/li><li>:67 sets <code>U=Clamp(landscape?Min(width/75.8f,height/35.7f):Min(width/31.7f,height/64.5f),8,17)<\/code>. Those constants are the HTML&#x27;s em extents.<\/li><li><code>E(em)=em<em>U<\/code> and <code>Z(em)=Max(7,Round(em<\/em>U))<\/code> (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.Chrome.cs:14,16<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>RuneBoardWindow.Render<\/code> uses the same constants on <code>shell.Frame.rect<\/code> (<code>P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:62-63<\/code>).<\/li><li>Neither fits a fixed design rect or centres margins. The plan §9.2 fit-and-centre 1:1 unit is new code.<\/li><li><strong>Root and canvas.<\/strong><\/li><li>Blacksmith creates <code>new GameObject(&quot;Blacksmith&quot;,typeof(RectTransform),typeof(Canvas),typeof(CanvasScaler),typeof(GraphicRaycaster))<\/code> under the GameUI transform, <code>ScreenSpaceOverlay<\/code>, <code>sortingOrder=320<\/code> (:30-31). Storage is 320, HuntEdict 310, RuneMaster 330.<\/li><li>The scaler is <code>ConstantPixelSize<\/code> with <code>scaleFactor=scale<\/code> (:68).<\/li><li>Reflow does <code>Clear(canvasRoot)<\/code> (destroys all children), adds a backdrop, then a <code>frame<\/code> anchored bottom-left at <code>safe.position/scale<\/code> with <code>RectMask2D<\/code> (:69-71).<\/li><li>On the host stack the host rewrites sorting to <code>400+i*10<\/code> and restores it on removal (<code>P/ContentWindowHost.cs:87,62<\/code>).<\/li><li>RuneBoard owns no canvas. <code>ContentWindowView.Open<\/code> (<code>P/ContentWindowView.cs:23-29<\/code>) builds it, and <code>Repaint<\/code> sets scaler and <code>Canvas.scaleFactor<\/code> (:38-40). <code>Render<\/code> hides the shell title, close, frame and scroll (<code>P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:64<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Reflow<\/strong> is polling, not events: <code>if(safe!=UiSafeArea.Current||language!=Loc.Language||Mathf.Abs(textScale-readingScale())&gt;.001f)Reflow();<\/code> (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:40<\/code>; same in <code>P/StorageWindow.cs:72-73<\/code>, <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:56<\/code>). Shell windows do it in <code>ContentWindowView.Update<\/code> (:30). <code>GameUI.ApplyLanguage<\/code> also repaints a fixed list of windows (<code>P/GameUI.cs:109<\/code>). <code>readingScale<\/code> is always 1 (<code>P/GameUI.cs:71<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Attach.<\/strong> <code>ContentWindowHost.Attach(Component owner,Action back,bool pause=true,bool blocksGameplay=true)<\/code> (:28) silently returns if the window is not under GameUI (:30). <code>StoreViewBinding.Attach(Component owner,GameStore store,Action refresh,Func&lt;bool&gt; ready=null,Func&lt;string&gt; visibleState=null)<\/code> is at <code>P/StoreViewBinding.cs:13<\/code>. Full real example, <code>P/StorageWindow.cs:67<\/code> and <code>:111-114<\/code>:<\/li><\/ul><pre><code>ContentWindowHost.Attach(view,view.Escape);StoreViewBinding.Attach(view,store,view.Repaint,()=&gt;view.modal==null&amp;&amp;!view.Dragging,view.DisplayKey);\nstring DisplayKey()=&gt;string.Join(&quot;|&quot;,StoreViewBinding.EquipmentKey(Account),Account.gold,Account.premium,Account.materials,\n  Account.gemCapacity,StoreViewBinding.Key(Account.warehouseCapacity),...,StoreViewBinding.Key(Account.contentUnlocks),badge?.Invoke());<\/code><\/pre><p>The Blacksmith call has no key (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:33<\/code>) and is grandfathered at <code>R/tools/check_ui_refresh.py:60-63<\/code>.<\/p><ul><li><strong>Back, pause, input.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>Push<\/code> adds a <code>CanvasGroup<\/code>, takes a ref-counted pause lease on the active <code>RunState<\/code>, and disables interaction on every other canvas under the host. Only the top window is interactable (<code>P/ContentWindowHost.cs:33-89<\/code>).<\/li><li>Escape calls the top entry&#x27;s <code>back<\/code> (:92-96). <code>ContentWindowHost.BackLocked<\/code> can veto (:22; set at <code>P/GameUI.TutorialStaging.cs:35<\/code>). Close with <code>Detach(this)<\/code>.<\/li><li>Inside the window, repaints are deferred while input is busy. <code>StoreViewBinding.InputBusy<\/code> (:43-50) covers press, <code>UiButton.Pressed<\/code>, a focused InputField and an open dropdown. RuneBoard defers repaint to <code>LateUpdate<\/code> while dragging (<code>P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:39-43<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>ADAPTERS entries<\/strong> (<code>R/tools/check_ui_contract.py:16-23<\/code>):<\/li><\/ul><pre><code>&#x27;BlacksmithWindow&#x27;: (&#x27;ContentWindowHost.Attach&#x27;,&#x27;UiTheme.Scale&#x27;,&#x27;EquipmentSlotView&#x27;,&#x27;CharacterEquipmentView&#x27;,&#x27;ItemDetailView&#x27;),\n&#x27;HuntEdictWindow&#x27;: (&#x27;ContentWindowHost.Attach&#x27;,&#x27;UiTheme.Scale&#x27;,&#x27;HuntEdictSummary&#x27;,&#x27;Session.Draft&#x27;),\n&#x27;RuneMasterWindow&#x27;: (&#x27;ContentWindowHost.Attach&#x27;,&#x27;UiFonts.Body&#x27;),<\/code><\/pre><p>Tokens are searched in comment-stripped source of <code>Owner.cs<\/code> plus <code>Owner.*.cs<\/code> (:51-58).<\/p><ul><li><strong>Alternative route.<\/strong> <code>RuneBoardWindow<\/code> (not in ADAPTERS) uses <code>ContentWindowView.Open<\/code> as its shell, so it needs no canvas exemption. The cost is hiding shell chrome (:64).<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"3-scrolling-and-input\">3. SCROLLING AND INPUT<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Scroll views.<\/strong><\/li><li>All are <code>ScrollRect<\/code> + clear <code>Image<\/code> + <code>RectMask2D<\/code> viewport, content anchored top, <code>Clamped<\/code>. Copies are at <code>P/ContentWindowView.cs:48-53<\/code>, <code>P/BlacksmithWindow.Controls.cs:32-42<\/code> (with <code>Scrollbar<\/code>), <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:265-277<\/code>, <code>P/RuneBoardWindow.cs:101-106<\/code>.<\/li><li>All set <code>horizontal=false<\/code>, except <code>HudStatusScroll<\/code> (horizontal only, no inertia, <code>P/StatusStripView.cs:10-17,41<\/code>) and the codex tab strip (<code>P/MonsterCodexWindow.cs:100<\/code>).<\/li><li>No ScrollRect with both axes exists.<\/li><li>Nested scroll is avoided by locking the outer one (<code>P/MonsterCodexWindow.Detail.cs:14<\/code>, <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:186<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Tap vs drag.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>UiButton<\/code> (<code>P/UiButton.cs:12-97<\/code>) has no drag logic. It relies on EventSystem, so a ScrollRect drag cancels the press. <code>Pressed<\/code> (:24) lets <code>StoreViewBinding<\/code> postpone repaints.<\/li><li>Custom cells forward gestures to the parent ScrollRect: <code>StorageCell<\/code> (<code>P/StorageWindow.Drag.cs:13-31<\/code>, with <code>!e.dragging<\/code> on click), <code>RuneMasterCell<\/code> (<code>P/RuneMasterWindow.Drag.cs:7-17<\/code>).<\/li><li>Direction arbitration: <code>TrainingChartView<\/code> hands off when <code>|dy|&gt;|dx|<\/code> (<code>P/TrainingChartView.cs:73-76<\/code>). <code>AttendanceSwipeTarget<\/code> decides after 10 px with a 1.25 ratio (<code>P/AttendanceSwipe.cs:32-53<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>HoldPress<\/code> separates a tap (&lt; 0.3 s) from a 0.7 s hold gauge (<code>P/HoldPress.cs:8-39<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>useDragThreshold<\/code> is set per control; <code>pixelDragThreshold<\/code> is never changed.<\/li><li><strong>Scroll preserved across Repaint<\/strong> is the owner&#x27;s job. Save <code>content.anchoredPosition.y<\/code>, rebuild, <code>Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases()<\/code>, clamp, restore. See <code>P/ContentWindowView.cs:33,62<\/code>, <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:188-195<\/code> (dictionary by key), <code>P/StorageWindow.cs:440-449<\/code>, <code>P/InventoryWindow.cs:77-79<\/code>.<\/li><li>Only Y is ever stored. X is never persisted anywhere.<\/li><li><code>StoreViewBinding<\/code> restores focus, not scroll (:25-39).<\/li><li>Scroll-into-view: <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:298-306<\/code>, and the smoke <code>Tap<\/code> (<code>P/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:54-65<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>UiVisibility.Visible/Fraction<\/code> (<code>P/UiVisibility.cs:13-28<\/code>) computes the reachable part of a control.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"4-text\">4. TEXT<\/h2><ul><li><strong><code>UiLayout.Text<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/UiTheme.cs:156-160<\/code>) sets <code>font??UiFonts.Body<\/code>, int <code>fontSize<\/code>, <code>supportRichText=true<\/code>, <code>raycastTarget=false<\/code>, <code>horizontalOverflow=Wrap<\/code> and <code>verticalOverflow=Truncate<\/code>. It leaves the default UpperLeft alignment, no <code>lineSpacing<\/code>, and does not call <code>Loc.T<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>HuntEdictWindow.Text<\/code> also runs <code>ClassSkillTree.Display<\/code> (<code>P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:70<\/code>), which swaps skill codes like W01 for names (<code>Runtime/Core/ClassSkillTree.cs:120<\/code>).<\/li><li>Adapters build their own Text, mostly with <code>supportRichText=false<\/code> (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.Controls.cs:16-20<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Fonts<\/strong> (<code>P/UiTheme.cs:131-147<\/code>):<\/li><li><code>Body<\/code> is an OS dynamic font from {Apple SD Gothic Neo, Malgun Gothic, Noto Sans CJK KR, Noto Sans CJK, Droid Sans Fallback, Arial}. WebGL uses the preloaded <code>ThirdParty/Fonts/NanumGothic-Regular.ttf<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Display<\/code> is {Baskerville, Georgia, Times New Roman, Noto Serif}, and WebGL uses Body.<\/li><li>Noto Serif KR and Cinzel are not bundled (plan D6).<\/li><li><code>check_ui_contract.py:61-62<\/code> rejects creating fonts outside <code>UiTheme.cs<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Shadow and outline<\/strong> are Unity <code>Shadow<\/code>/<code>Outline<\/code> with hard offsets only: <code>P/ItemDetailView.Style.cs:140<\/code>, <code>P/GlobalHudView.cs:207<\/code>, <code>P/AttendanceWindow.cs:182<\/code>, <code>P/TitleScreenView.cs:39<\/code>, <code>Outline<\/code> at <code>P/GameUI.Plaza.cs:106<\/code>. Rich text is <code>&lt;color=#hex&gt;<\/code> in 6 places (e.g. <code>P/EquipmentComparisonView.cs:19<\/code>); there is no <code>&lt;size&gt;<\/code> or <code>&lt;b&gt;<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Gradient-filled text<\/strong> does not exist anywhere.<\/li><li><strong>Line height and wrapping.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>Text.lineSpacing<\/code> is a multiplier of the font&#x27;s own line height (set to 1 or 1.12: <code>P/ItemDetailView.Style.cs:30<\/code>, <code>P/StorageWindow.cs:469<\/code>). There is no CSS px line-height.<\/li><li>No keep-all control exists. A grep for NBSP, ZWSP and word-joiner characters across <code>Runtime<\/code> finds nothing.<\/li><li>Wrapping is only checked via <code>cachedTextGenerator.lineCount<\/code> and <code>preferredHeight<\/code> in smokes (<code>P/RuntimeJewelerSmoke.cs:57-58<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>resizeTextForBestFit<\/code> is the usual overflow fix (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.Controls.cs:25<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Measurement helpers<\/strong> that could replace the HTML&#x27;s <code>tw()<\/code>/<code>fitFs()<\/code> (<code>D/SkillWindow.dc.html:486-497<\/code>):<\/li><li><code>Text.preferredWidth/Height<\/code> (<code>P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:111<\/code>, <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:105<\/code>).<\/li><li>Throwaway-Text <code>TextWidth(value,size,bold,serif)<\/code> and <code>TextHeight(value,w,size,bold)<\/code> (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.Chrome.cs:41-51<\/code>).<\/li><li>Static, no GameObject: <code>t.cachedTextGeneratorForLayout.GetPreferredWidth(value,t.GetGenerationSettings(Vector2.zero))/t.pixelsPerUnit<\/code> (<code>P/GameUI.Rift.cs:70-71<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>new TextGenerator().GetPreferredWidth(value,new TextGenerationSettings{font=UiFonts.Body,fontSize=size,fontStyle=FontStyle.Normal,scaleFactor=1,richText=true})<\/code> (<code>P/MonsterCodexWindow.cs:129<\/code>).<\/li><li>Set <code>Canvas.scaleFactor<\/code> before measuring on a first render (<code>P/ContentWindowView.cs:39-40<\/code>).<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"5-animation\">5. ANIMATION<\/h2><p>There is no tween library. Everything is <code>Update<\/code> or a coroutine on <code>Time.unscaledTime<\/code> or <code>unscaledDeltaTime<\/code>, because pause is <code>RunState.paused<\/code>, not <code>timeScale<\/code>.<\/p><ul><li><strong><code>UiButtonFace<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/UiButtonFace.cs:21,39,43-49<\/code>): a state change sets progress to 0, and <code>Update<\/code> lerps the palette and calls <code>SetVerticesDirty<\/code> each step. <code>Show<\/code> early-outs when nothing changed (:30-31), so a repeated Repaint does not restart it.<\/li><li><strong><code>ForgeWorkingPulse<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.Slots.cs:245-250<\/code>): a CanvasGroup alpha of <code>.65+.35<em>cos(unscaledTime<\/em>2π/1.5)<\/code>, with no mesh rebuild. It reads PlayerPrefs each frame.<\/li><li><strong><code>TutorialAnchorRing<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/TutorialAnchorRing.cs:17-36<\/code>): <code>Update()=&gt;SetVerticesDirty()<\/code> every frame. It has a breathing border, ripple and bobbing pointer, and is still under reduce-motion (:20).<\/li><li><strong><code>AttendanceClaimGlow<\/code><\/strong> is a static mesh.<\/li><li><strong><code>ContentDockView<\/code><\/strong> (<code>P/GameUI.ContentDock.cs:73-112<\/code>): <code>Seconds=.22f<\/code>, step = <code>Time.unscaledDeltaTime/Seconds<\/code>, with a <code>Settled<\/code> early-out and <code>Snap(bool)<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Window tickers:<\/strong><\/li><li><code>RuneMasterWindow.TickFusion<\/code> (<code>P/RuneMasterWindow.cs:173-184<\/code>): start time, <code>SmoothStep<\/code>, <code>Lerp<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>RiftRewardRevealMotion<\/code> (<code>P/RiftRewardRevealWindow.cs:42-47<\/code>): scale .86 to 1 plus alpha.<\/li><li><code>DialogueEntrance<\/code> (<code>P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:44-51<\/code>).<\/li><li>Blacksmith&#x27;s 0.25 s ticker (<code>P/BlacksmithWindow.cs:43-49<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Cheap alpha:<\/strong> <code>canvasRenderer.SetAlpha<\/code> (<code>P/UiButton.cs:63,68<\/code>) and CanvasGroup do not rebuild meshes.<\/li><li><strong>Reduce motion:<\/strong> <code>WorldLighting.ReduceMotionKey=&quot;hellscript.reduce-motion&quot;<\/code> (<code>P/WorldLighting.cs:46<\/code>) is a PlayerPrefs int. <code>StoryDialogueWindow.ReduceMotion<\/code> is that flag OR <code>SystemReduceMotion<\/code> (<code>P/StoryDialogueWindow.cs:55<\/code>).<\/li><li>The OS flag is read only on macOS via objc, cached 1 s (:57-70), and is <code>false<\/code> elsewhere (:72).<\/li><li>No settings UI writes the key (comment <code>P/WorldLighting.cs:44-45<\/code>), and <code>ForgeWorkingPulse<\/code> ignores the OS flag.<\/li><li><strong>Pooled floating numbers:<\/strong> no UI one exists. The nearest pools are the <code>StatusStripView<\/code> entries (<code>P/StatusStripView.cs:21,75-77<\/code>), <code>PrologueGate<\/code> <code>DimPool=16<\/code> (<code>P/PrologueGate.cs:16,31<\/code>), and the capped, oldest-recycled 3D <code>WorldFx<\/code> transients (<code>P/WorldFx.cs:13-31<\/code>).<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"6-smoke-and-screenshot-framework\">6. SMOKE AND SCREENSHOT FRAMEWORK<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Structure.<\/strong><\/li><li>A smoke is a <code>MonoBehaviour<\/code> in <code>P/Runtime<em>Smoke<\/em>.cs<\/code>, wrapped in <code>#if UNITY_EDITOR || DEVELOPMENT_BUILD<\/code>.<\/li><li>A <code>[RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod(AfterSceneLoad)] static void Boot()<\/code> returns unless <code>Debug.isDebugBuild<\/code> and the flag is in <code>GetCommandLineArgs()<\/code>. It sets <code>Application.runInBackground=true<\/code> and creates the GameObject (<code>P/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:42-47<\/code>, <code>P/RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke.cs:210-217<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>P/RuntimeBlacksmithSmoke.cs:20-26<\/code> also sets <code>InputSystem.settings.backgroundBehavior=IgnoreFocus<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Start()<\/code> is a coroutine. It reads <code>-hellscriptSavePath<\/code> (required) and <code>-hellscriptScreenshots<\/code>, <code>-hellscriptEvidence<\/code> or <code>-hellscriptEvidencePath<\/code> (<code>P/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:106-109<\/code>; the three names vary per smoke). It then waits 1 s and calls <code>FindAnyObjectByType&lt;GameController&gt;()<\/code>.<\/li><li>Failures: an exception writes <code>failure.txt<\/code> and calls <code>Quit(1)<\/code> (:48-51). Success writes <code>runtime.txt<\/code> or an <code>..._OK<\/code> marker such as <code>HELLSCRIPT_BATTLEQUICK_SMOKE_OK<\/code> (<code>P/RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke.cs:343-344<\/code>).<\/li><li>Files starting <code>Runtime<\/code> and containing <code>Smoke<\/code> are skipped by both UI check tools (<code>check_ui_contract.py:52<\/code>, <code>check_ui_refresh.py:51<\/code>) and by <code>LocalizationTests<\/code> (<code>T/LocalizationTests.cs:259<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Helpers<\/strong> (copied per smoke, not shared):<\/li><li><code>Require(bool,string)<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Find(name)<\/code> (:52).<\/li><li><code>Bounds(RectTransform)<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Tap(name)<\/code> scrolls the button&#x27;s ScrollRect to centre, then calls <code>TapAt<\/code> (:54-65).<\/li><li><code>TapAt(Vector2,name)<\/code> calls <code>EventSystem.current.RaycastAll<\/code>, requires the first hit to be the button, then runs <code>ExecuteEvents.Execute<\/code> for pointerDown, pointerUp and pointerClick (:71-81).<\/li><li><code>Hold(target,seconds)<\/code> (BattleQuick :29-33).<\/li><li>Waits: <code>yield return null<\/code> twice, or <code>WaitForSecondsRealtime(.25f)<\/code> plus <code>Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases()<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Resize(w,h,lang)<\/code> (:82-87): <code>game.ApplyLanguage(lang); game.UI.RefreshCanvasLayout(); Screen.SetResolution(w,h,Windowed)<\/code>, poll up to 8 s, then 0.4 s.<\/li><li><code>Capture(name)<\/code> (:88-89): <code>Debug.developerConsoleVisible=false; Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases(); WaitForEndOfFrame; ScreenCapture.CaptureScreenshotAsTexture()<\/code>, then <code>EncodeToPNG<\/code> and <code>File.WriteAllBytes<\/code>. RuneBoard uses <code>CaptureScreenshot(path)<\/code> (<code>P/RuntimeRuneBoardSmoke.cs:40<\/code>).<\/li><li>Real mouse device: <code>InputSystem.AddDevice&lt;Mouse&gt;<\/code> (<code>P/RuntimeRuneBoardSmoke.cs:94<\/code>).<\/li><li>Notch: <code>UiSafeArea.Simulate(left,bottom,right,top)<\/code> (debug builds only, <code>P/UiSafeArea.cs:59-61<\/code>) and <code>StopSimulating()<\/code>. The plan&#x27;s iPhone insets are already used at <code>P/RuntimeScreenSettingsSmoke.RiftTitle.cs:69<\/code> (956 wide: 62/21/62/0; 440 wide: 0/34/0/62).<\/li><li><code>UiSafeArea.AspectRatio=0<\/code> resets the aspect frame (<code>P/RuntimeRuneBoardSmoke.cs:45<\/code>).<\/li><li>Resume: a second launch with the same save path and <code>-hellscriptSkillTreeResume<\/code> asserts persisted state, writes <code>restart.txt<\/code> and quits (:118-125).<\/li><li><strong>Exact commands<\/strong> (clone with <code>cp -Rc Assets Packages ProjectSettings Library &lt;work&gt;/proj; rm -f &lt;work&gt;/proj/Temp/UnityLockfile<\/code>; Unity 6000.6.0f1). <code>-nographics<\/code> and <code>-logFile<\/code> are from <code>CPU_Optimization_20261002.md:120<\/code>; the Unity binary path is from <code>R/tools/hunyuan_monster_install.py:31<\/code>.<\/li><\/ul><pre><code>/Applications/Unity/Hub/Editor/6000.6.0f1/Unity.app/Contents/MacOS/Unity -batchmode -nographics -quit -projectPath &lt;work&gt;/proj -buildTarget StandaloneOSX -executeMethod Hellscript.Editor.ProjectBuilder.BuildMac -hellscriptBuildOutput &lt;out&gt;/HELLSCRIPT.app -logFile &lt;out&gt;/build.log\nARGS=(-hellscriptSkillTreeD4Smoke -hellscriptOfflineQa -hellscriptSavePath &quot;$SAVE&quot; -hellscriptScreenshots &quot;$SHOTS&quot; -screen-fullscreen 0 -screen-width 440 -screen-height 956); &lt;out&gt;/HELLSCRIPT.app/Contents/MacOS/HELLSCRIPT &quot;${ARGS[@]}&quot;<\/code><\/pre><p><code>BuildMac<\/code> is a development build (<code>E/ProjectBuilder.cs:68-71,78-95<\/code>) and the output must end in <code>.app<\/code> (:110-121). Use bash arrays; zsh does not split words. <code>-hellscriptOfflineQa<\/code> is only needed for flows that start at the title.<\/p><ul><li><strong>What the docs say.<\/strong><\/li><li>No &quot;Smoke build recipe&quot; heading exists. <code>R/Docs/Design/Hunt_Edict_UI_Overhaul.en.md:577-582<\/code> (§12.6) says AGENTS.md has none and lists the steps used locally.<\/li><li>Command lines are in <code>Docs/Implementation/Map_Display_Option.md:134-138<\/code>, <code>Town_Hunyuan_Models.md:109<\/code> and <code>Blacksmith_Validation.md:149<\/code>. Plan §15 is <code>D4_Skill_Tree_Plan_20261012.md:506<\/code> and the smoke spec is :460-471.<\/li><li>No script automates smokes. The only runner in the repo is <code>R/tools/profile_native_cpu.py<\/code> (CPU profile). The <code>run_smokes.py<\/code> named in that doc is not in the repo.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"7-editmode-ui-tests\">7. EDITMODE UI TESTS<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Building uGUI in EditMode.<\/strong><\/li><li>Create <code>new GameObject(&quot;x&quot;,typeof(RectTransform),typeof(Canvas))<\/code>, add an <code>EventSystem<\/code> child for pointer tests (<code>T/UiButtonTests.cs:13-20<\/code>, <code>T/StoreViewBindingTests.cs:19-31<\/code>), or make a <code>ContentWindowHost<\/code> root, then call the real <code>Open(...)<\/code> (<code>T/SharedUiTests.cs:63<\/code>, <code>T/MonsterCodexWindowTests.cs:14-23<\/code>).<\/li><li>Measure <code>RectTransform.rect<\/code>, <code>Text.preferredHeight<\/code> and <code>Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases()<\/code>.<\/li><li>Vary layout by <code>UiSafeArea.AspectRatio=w/(float)h<\/code> (the frame is fitted inside the Game view, <code>P/UiSafeArea.cs:25-26<\/code>).<\/li><li><code>T/MonsterCodexWindowTests.cs:43-62<\/code> is the pattern: five sizes by ko/en, asserting row counts, tap targets &gt;= 44 px, <code>preferredHeight&lt;=rect.height+.5<\/code> and <code>Loc.MissingCount==0<\/code>. English comes from <code>Loc.Use(&quot;en&quot;,LocalizationTable.Parse(Resources.Load&lt;TextAsset&gt;(&quot;Localization/en&quot;).text).Entries)<\/code>. TearDown resets <code>AspectRatio=0<\/code>, <code>StopSimulating()<\/code> and <code>Loc.UseSource()<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>TouchLayoutTests<\/code> is pure maths on <code>Runtime/Core/TouchLayout.cs<\/code>, with no GameObjects.<\/li><li>Pure-layout precedent: <code>BattleHudLayout<\/code>/<code>InventoryLayout<\/code> with <code>[TestCaseSource]<\/code> (<code>T/BattleHudLayoutTests.cs:9-26<\/code>), a good template for the plan&#x27;s layout function.<\/li><li><code>T/GraphicComponentTests.cs:13-24<\/code> reflects over every <code>Graphic<\/code> subclass: each needs <code>[RequireComponent(typeof(CanvasRenderer))]<\/code>, and <code>AddComponent(type)<\/code> with no setup must not throw.<\/li><li><strong>Mesh golden and allocation test:<\/strong> <code>T/ForgePresentationAllocationTests.cs:13-24,54-68<\/code> reflects <code>OnPopulateMesh<\/code> into a delegate and compares <code>vertices<\/code>, <code>colors32<\/code> and <code>triangles<\/code> with <code>T/Fixtures/forge-ring-baseline-N.json<\/code>. It then asserts <code>Is.Not.AllocatingGCMemory()<\/code> after warm-up.<\/li><li><strong>Loading repo files.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>File.ReadAllText(Path.Combine(Application.dataPath,&quot;..&quot;,&quot;Docs/Design/MonsterRoster/roster.json&quot;))<\/code> (<code>T/MonsterSoakTests.cs:16<\/code>).<\/li><li>CWD-relative <code>File.ReadAllText(&quot;Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Fixtures/RuneNativeParity.json&quot;)<\/code> with <code>JsonUtility<\/code> and <code>[Serializable]<\/code> classes (<code>T/RuneBoardNativeTests.cs:18<\/code>). This is a JS-to-C# parity fixture.<\/li><li><code>Path.Combine(Application.dataPath,&quot;HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Fixtures/RuneV13Layout.json&quot;)<\/code> (<code>T/RuneV13Tests.cs:67<\/code>).<\/li><li>There is no <code>InternalsVisibleTo<\/code>, so tests see only public members or use <code>BindingFlags.NonPublic<\/code> reflection (<code>T/StoreViewBindingTests.cs:18<\/code>).<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"8-icons-and-masks\">8. ICONS AND MASKS<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Crop.<\/strong> A circular crop is a <code>Plate<\/code> <code>Image<\/code> with sprite <code>Art/GlobalHUD/mask-circle<\/code> and a stencil <code>Mask<\/code> (<code>showMaskGraphic=true<\/code>). The child <code>Icon<\/code> is an <code>Image<\/code> with <code>preserveAspect=true<\/code> (<code>P/SkillIconView.cs:28-35,41-46<\/code>). Passives use <code>mask-square<\/code> and <code>frame-active<\/code>. The HUD seal uses the same approach with <code>showMaskGraphic=false<\/code> (<code>P/GlobalHudView.cs:178-183<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Masks.<\/strong> They are 256² white RGBA sprites, bilinear. <code>mask-square<\/code> is a rounded square and <code>mask-circle<\/code> is a circle. A frame image (<code>frame-seal<\/code>, <code>frame-active<\/code>) covers the hard stencil edge.<\/li><li><strong>Skill icons.<\/strong> <code>Resources/Art/ClassSkillIcons/{Warrior,Ranger,Mage}/&lt;id&gt;.png<\/code>: 37 each, 1254², no mipmaps, not readable.<\/li><li><strong>Budget rows.<\/strong> <code>E/ResourceTextureBudget.cs:24<\/code> is Android 512 ASTC_6x6. The desktop table (<code>:63-82<\/code>, <code>Art/ClassSkillIcons/<\/code> 512) gives Standalone BC7 and WebGL ETC2_RGBA8. <code>Art/SkillTree/<\/code> has its own rows (<code>tree-backdrop<\/code> 1024, rest 512). Masks and frames have no row.<\/li><li><strong>Tests.<\/strong> <code>T/BuildResourceTests.cs:11-32<\/code> checks one icon sample for overrides plus GUID/meta stability; <code>P/RuntimeBuildResourceSmoke.cs:20-27<\/code> samples at runtime.<\/li><li><strong>Old tree art<\/strong> (<code>Art/SkillTree/node-frame-*<\/code>, <code>tree-backdrop<\/code>, <code>skill-point-gem<\/code>) is used at <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs:25,77,86,232-241<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>New ids.<\/strong> The 84 modifier ids are unknown to <code>TryResolve<\/code>. Extend it, or <code>Resources.Load<\/code> the sprite and call <code>SetSprite<\/code>.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"9-fileassembly-conventions\">9. FILE/ASSEMBLY CONVENTIONS<\/h2><ul><li><strong>Layout.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>P/<\/code> is flat (493 <code>.cs<\/code> files, 157 of them smokes). Namespace is <code>Hellscript<\/code>.<\/li><li>There are three asmdefs: <code>Runtime/Hellscript.Runtime.asmdef<\/code> (all of Core, Presentation and Runes), <code>Editor/Hellscript.Editor.asmdef<\/code>, and <code>Tests/Editor/Hellscript.Tests.asmdef<\/code> (Editor only).<\/li><li>Partial naming is <code>X.cs<\/code> (Open, Update, Reflow) plus <code>X.&lt;Topic&gt;.cs<\/code>, as in <code>BlacksmithWindow.Chrome/Controls/Slots.cs<\/code> and <code>HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs<\/code>. Use <code>SkillTreeD4Window<em>.cs<\/code> and <code>RuntimeSkillTreeD4Smoke<\/em>.cs<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Registration in GameUI.<\/strong> Add a partial <code>GameUI.&lt;Name&gt;.cs<\/code>:<\/li><li>Follow <code>P/GameUI.Blacksmith.cs:5-21<\/code>, <code>GameUI.RuneBoard.cs<\/code> and <code>GameUI.AspectStone.cs<\/code>: field, public accessor for smokes, <code>Show…()<\/code> and <code>Close…()<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>Show…()<\/code> gates with <code>RequireContent(...)<\/code>, closes sibling windows (<code>CloseRuneMaster();CloseBlacksmith();CloseHudPanel();CloseStorage();CloseEquipmentShop();ResetTownInput();game.Town.Cancel()<\/code>), then calls <code>Open(transform,…)<\/code> with a <code>closed<\/code> callback that nulls the field and runs <code>RefreshHud();RefreshPlaza();<\/code>.<\/li><li>The host is created at <code>P/GameUI.cs:38<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>CommonPanelOpen<\/code> (<code>P/GameUI.ScreenSettings.cs:22<\/code>) picks up <code>windowHost.BlocksGameplay<\/code> automatically.<\/li><li>Language: add to the <code>P/GameUI.cs:109<\/code> chain, or poll in <code>Update<\/code>.<\/li><li>Entry points to repoint: <code>P/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:69<\/code>, <code>P/GameUI.FirstPlay.cs:22<\/code>, <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.SkillPresets.cs:59<\/code>, <code>P/HuntEdictWindow.cs:60<\/code>, <code>P/RiftEntryWindow.cs:355<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Template.<\/strong> <code>R/tools/new_content_ui.py<\/code> plus <code>R/tools/templates/ContentWindow.cs.txt<\/code> emits a static <code>&lt;Name&gt;Window<\/code> that calls <code>ContentWindowView.Open<\/code>. That is the route that needs no ADAPTERS entry.<\/li><li><strong><code>check_ui_contract.py<\/code> failures<\/strong> (<code>R/tools/check_ui_contract.py<\/code>):<\/li><li><code>{owner}: missing shared owner {token}<\/code> (:58).<\/li><li><code>{name}: use UiFonts instead of creating a font<\/code> (:62).<\/li><li><code>{name}: new content must open ContentWindowView; specialized layouts require a reviewed adapter<\/code> (:67): any <code>class \\w+Window<\/code> whose owner is not in ADAPTERS and has no <code>ContentWindowView.Open<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>{name}: canvas ownership belongs to ContentWindowView/ContentWindowHost<\/code> (:70): <code>AddComponent&lt;Canvas&gt;<\/code> or <code>typeof(Canvas)<\/code> outside ADAPTERS or <code>CANVAS_OWNERS<\/code> (:25-26).<\/li><li><code>{name}: chrome colour {hex} must use a UiTheme token<\/code> (:77): any <code>&quot;rrggbb&quot;<\/code> or <code>&quot;rrggbbaa&quot;<\/code> string literal that <code>chrome_colour()<\/code> (:33-42) judges warm, dark or ivory. By that function, <code>b9c6d0<\/code>, <code>fff3d6<\/code> and <code>d3af72<\/code> fail, while <code>6f8291<\/code> and <code>e07a32<\/code> pass. The rule is heuristic, so put every design colour in <code>UiTheme.cs<\/code> (exempt, :31).<\/li><li><code>reusable views cannot mutate or read a live account<\/code> for <code>PURE_VIEWS<\/code> (:78-79).<\/li><li><code>test_ui_contract.py:22<\/code> runs the same check on a copy of the whole Presentation folder.<\/li><li><strong><code>check_ui_refresh.py:55-66<\/code>:<\/strong> <code>{path}:{line}: define visibleState or an audited owner guard<\/code>. Every <code>StoreViewBinding.Attach<\/code> in a top-level <code>P/<em>.cs<\/code> needs &gt;= 5 arguments or <code>visibleState:<\/code>. It scans only top-level files and skips <code>Runtime<\/em><\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Source-scanning EditMode tests.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>T/LocalizationTests.cs:239-255<\/code>: every non-interpolated Korean literal in Runtime (smokes excluded) needs an exact <code>en.txt<\/code> entry, and interpolated Korean fails.<\/li><li><code>T/EditorNullPatternTests.cs:41-49<\/code>: no <code>GetComponent…() ??<\/code> or <code>?.<\/code>; use <code>TryGetComponent<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>T/GraphicComponentTests.cs<\/code> (see section 7).<\/li><li><strong>Docs.<\/strong> <code>Shared_UI_Contract(.en).md<\/code> has a section per adapter; :108 is the old skill-tree adapter. <code>AgentRules/Shared_UI.md:12<\/code> requires the exception&#x27;s reason and verification to be written down.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"risks\">RISKS<\/h2><ol><li><strong>Font.<\/strong> Legacy <code>Text<\/code> has an int <code>fontSize<\/code>, so the design&#x27;s 10.5, 12.5 and 14.5 pt sizes round. Noto Serif KR and Cinzel are not available, and <code>UiFonts.Display<\/code> varies by OS. Line-height is a font-metric multiplier, and there is no letter-spacing or keep-all. Gradient title text and glow need new code.<\/li><li><strong>No anti-aliasing on custom meshes.<\/strong> Only <code>HuntEdictSurface<\/code> has a feather fringe. Hex, arc and round shapes will look jagged without one. <code>UiMesh<\/code> also lacks hairline snapping except where <code>px=1/canvas.scaleFactor<\/code> is copied (<code>P/UiButtonFace.cs:55-56<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Colour space.<\/strong> <code>ProjectSettings.asset:49<\/code> is Linear (<code>m_ActiveColorSpace: 1<\/code>). Alpha compositing and gradients can differ from CSS gamma blending, and nothing in the repo verifies this.<\/li><li><strong>Filters.<\/strong><\/li><li>Blur, grayscale, brightness and soft drop-shadow have no engine path. A new shader needs Stencil and <code>_ClipRect<\/code> support, which <code>PuzzleHubTone<\/code> lacks.<\/li><li>Skill icons are non-readable and have no mips, so baked blur is impossible, and plan §16 forbids touching icons.<\/li><li><strong>Clipping.<\/strong> <code>RectMask2D<\/code> plates clip outer glows and the design&#x27;s out-of-box ornaments (<code>gx-pan-*<\/code> at <code>top:-12px<\/code>). These need an unclipped layer above the scroll.<\/li><li><strong>Performance.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>UiMesh<\/code> helpers allocate, so any per-frame rebuild (ignite, glint, ring bloom) needs allocation-free dedicated Graphics.<\/li><li>Per-icon stencil <code>Mask<\/code> (<code>SkillIconView<\/code>) breaks batching across about 48 icons.<\/li><li>Moving scroll content re-batches the whole canvas.<\/li><li><code>AGENTS.md<\/code> and <code>CPU_Performance.md<\/code> forbid steady per-frame work.<\/li><li><strong>Scale mismatch.<\/strong> <code>UiTheme.Scale<\/code> bases are 800x450 and 405x720, and the Blacksmith U is clamped 8-17. The design is 1:1 px (440x860, 832x419, 1152x648 stages), so a new fit-and-centre scale is needed. <code>UiTheme.Scale<\/code> must still be called somewhere real (not in a comment) to satisfy the ADAPTERS token.<\/li><li><strong>Scroll.<\/strong> No two-axis or X-persisting scroll exists. Nested scroll is avoided by locking the outer one. The landscape plate&#x27;s right-edge fade has a precedent only in <code>GlobalHudFade.shader<\/code> (<code>P/StatusStripView.cs:46<\/code>).<\/li><li><strong>Reduce motion.<\/strong> No toggle writes the key, the OS flag is macOS only, and <code>ForgeWorkingPulse<\/code> ignores it. Use <code>StoryDialogueWindow.ReduceMotion<\/code>.<\/li><li><strong>Screenshot comparison.<\/strong> References are 2x (880x1912, 1912x880, 2880x1620). <code>macRetinaSupport:1<\/code> and <code>resizableWindow:0<\/code> (<code>ProjectSettings.asset:89,104<\/code>) mean oversized windows may be clamped. A capture strategy is needed; nothing in the repo automates smokes or the side-by-side comparison.<\/li><li><strong>Mask radius.<\/strong> <code>mask-square<\/code> radius is fixed (about 13%) while the design&#x27;s radii differ per widget. The stencil edge is hard. A UV-mesh crop (gap 9) is the alternative.<\/li><li><strong>Texture weight.<\/strong> 92 new 512² icons are about 24 MB each for BC7 (desktop) and ETC2 (WebGL), not the 11 MB APK-only figure in plan §11.<\/li><li><strong>Gating and lint.<\/strong><\/li><li><code>SkillIconAssets<\/code> does not resolve new ids.<\/li><li>A localization entry is needed for every Korean literal.<\/li><li>New colours must be <code>UiTheme<\/code> tokens (the lint is heuristic).<\/li><li><code>GetComponent … ?.<\/code> is banned.<\/li><li>Pre-existing worktree edits and the uncommitted <code>D/golden/<\/code> mean tests reading goldens depend on commit state.<\/li><\/ol>", "headings": [{"id": "1-drawing-primitives", "title": "1. DRAWING PRIMITIVES"}, {"id": "2-custom-unit-adapter-windows", "title": "2. CUSTOM-UNIT ADAPTER WINDOWS"}, {"id": "3-scrolling-and-input", "title": "3. SCROLLING AND INPUT"}, {"id": "4-text", "title": "4. TEXT"}, {"id": "5-animation", "title": "5. ANIMATION"}, {"id": "6-smoke-and-screenshot-framework", "title": "6. SMOKE AND SCREENSHOT FRAMEWORK"}, {"id": "7-editmode-ui-tests", "title": "7. EDITMODE UI TESTS"}, {"id": "8-icons-and-masks", "title": "8. ICONS AND MASKS"}, {"id": "9-fileassembly-conventions", "title": "9. FILE/ASSEMBLY CONVENTIONS"}, {"id": "risks", "title": "RISKS"}]}];
